From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:58:47 +0100
Subject: drm/lima: do not handle a GP MMU fault as an out-of-heap condition

A GP job whose PLBU allocates from a growable heap BO is marked
recoverable. lima_sched_pipe_task_done() then sends every error of such
a job to the recover work, including a page fault reported by the GP MMU
through lima_gp_task_mmu_error(). The recover work grows the heap and
restarts the PLBU allocation, but the MMU stays in page fault mode, so
the job stalls until the scheduler timeout (10 s by default) fires.

Clear the recoverable flag on an MMU fault, so that the job is reset at
once like a non-heap job.

Fixes: 2081e8dcf1ee ("drm/lima: recover task by enlarging heap buffer")
Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/lima/lima_gp.c
@@ -230,6 +230,12 @@ static void lima_gp_task_error(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 
 static void lima_gp_task_mmu_error(struct lima_sched_pipe *pipe)
 {
+	struct lima_sched_task *task = pipe->current_task;
+
+	/* a heap grow does not resume a faulted MMU: reset the job at once */
+	if (task)
+		task->recoverable = false;
+
 	lima_sched_pipe_task_done(pipe);
 }
 
